    "https://www.lr.edu/work-at-lr": {
      "title": "Work",
      "description": "Work at LR | Lenoir-Rhyne University Jump to Header Jump to Main Content Jump to Footer Return to home Open Menu Open Search Search Search Close Search Admission & Aid Click to toggle child links Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Seminary Admission Financial Aid & Costs LR Tuition-Free Guarantee College Affordability Paying Your Bill Academics Click to toggle child links Undergraduate Programs Graduate & Doctoral Programs Seminary Programs BEAR Central & Academic Support Research & Scholarship Study Abroad & International Education Internships & Careers Centers & Institutes Registrar Library Student Experience Click to toggle child links Activities & Organizations Athletics Health & Wellness Residence Life Leadership & Service Religious & Spiritual Life Campus Safety Dean of Students Belonging at LR Student Support & Outreach LR Experience Athletics About Click to toggle child links Fast Facts History & Traditions University Leadership Strategic Plan Accreditation Directory Offices & Services Community Partners Resources for Alumni Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Apply Visit Request Info Give Close Menu Home Page Work at LR Work at LR Join our community. At Lenoir-Rhyne, one of our greatest resources is our community of people. We believe every member of the university plays an essential role in supporting our mission and making a lasting impact on students’ lives. Explore our career opportunities and join the Lenoir-Rhyne community. At Lenoir-Rhyne, your work matters—you’ll be valued, supported and inspired to grow personally and professionally. Together, we foster a culture of collaboration, innovation and service that strengthens our students and our communities. Play video Be Part of Something Bigger Your career at Lenoir-Rhyne is more than a role. It’s being part of a supportive community dedicated to education, service and making a lasting impact together. Faculty Assistant Professor, Occupational Therapy Founding Director, Master of Science in Applied Behavior Analysis Teaching Assistant Professor, Counseling Asheville Teaching Assistant Professor, Counseling *All positions are located in Hickory unless otherwise noted. Part-time (immediate openings) Anatomy and Physiology Chemistry Communication Studies Languages Mathematics Occupational Therapy, M.S. Physics Sign Language Part-time (faculty pool) College of Business and Economics College of Fine Arts and Communication College of Humanities and Social Sciences College of Natural Sciences and Mathematics School of Counseling and Human Services School of Education School of Health, Exercise and Sport Science Asheville College of Humanities and Social Sciences School of Counseling and Human Services Staff Staff positions include part-time, full-time and athletics. All positions are located in Hickory unless otherwise noted. Assistant Director for Student Support and Outreach Director of Corporate Partnership Services Director of Creative and Digital Media, Athletics ERP/SIS Implementation Business Analyst Executive Assistant to the Provost Help Desk Support Assistant Learning Experience Designer Production Manager Public Safety Officer, Part-Time Youth Chorus Accompanist Youth Chorus Artistic Director Graduate Assistantships A graduate assistant (GA) is part-time position (recommended 20 hours of work per week, maximum 29 hours), that provides employment experience and the benefit of partial-tuition remission. In most, but not all cases, 15 free credit hours of tuition are provided to the GA for the duration of the position appointment period, which is typically August 1-July 31. Please Note : You must be enrolled as a graduate student at Lenoir-Rhyne to apply for a GA position. *All GA positions are located in Hickory unless otherwise noted. Graduate Assistant, Academic Support Services Graduate Assistant, Advising Center Graduate Assistant, Fritz Honors College Graduate Assistant, Marketing and Communications Graduate Assistant, NSF Robert Noyce Teacher Scholarship Program Graduate Assistant, Operations and Academic Recovery Graduate Assistant, Soccer - Goalkeeper Coach Graduate Assistant, Study Hall and Student-Athlete Support Notice of Non-Discrimination, Harassment and Anti-Retaliation Lenoir-Rhyne University is committed to providing a workplace and educational environment, as well as other benefits, programs and activities that are free from discrimination, harassment and retaliation. LR is committed to creating a safe campus environment for all members of the LR community, including, but not limited to, those who identify as transgender and gender non-conforming. To that end, LR does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, sex (including sex stereotypes and sex characteristics), ethnicity, national origin, physical or mental disability, age, marital status, pregnancy or related conditions, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, veteran or military status or any other characteristic or status protected by applicable law. To ensure compliance with federal and state civil rights laws and regulations and to affirm its commitment to promoting the goals of fairness and equity in all aspects of the educational program, activity and employment, LR has developed internal policies and procedures that provide a prompt, fair and impartial process for those involved in an allegation of discrimination or harassment, and for allegations of retaliation. LR values and upholds the equal dignity of all members of its community and strives to balance the rights of the parties in the grievance process during what is often a difficult time for all those involved. Work at LR Benefits Summary TimelyCare Virtual Health & Wellbeing Faculty & Staff Holidays Human Resources Related Links Notice of Non-Discrimination, Harassment and Anti-Retaliation Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Get Info Visit Apply Deposit Return to home Find us on Facebook Subscribe on YouTube Follow us on Instagram 625 7th Ave NE, Hickory, NC 28601 828.328.1741 Directory Virtual Tour, Maps & Directions Events Calendar University News Profile Magazine Work at LR Library Bookstore Copyright Privacy Policy Accessibility Title IX Safety & Emergency Preparedness Consumer Information Coronavirus © 2026 Lenoir-Rhyne University"
    },
    "https://www.lr.edu/admission-and-aid/paying-your-bill/pay-your-deposit": {
      "title": "Pay Your Deposit",
      "description": "Pay Your Deposit | Lenoir-Rhyne University Jump to Header Jump to Main Content Jump to Footer Return to home Open Menu Open Search Search Search Close Search Admission & Aid Click to toggle child links Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Seminary Admission Financial Aid & Costs LR Tuition-Free Guarantee College Affordability Paying Your Bill Academics Click to toggle child links Undergraduate Programs Graduate & Doctoral Programs Seminary Programs BEAR Central & Academic Support Research & Scholarship Study Abroad & International Education Internships & Careers Centers & Institutes Registrar Library Student Experience Click to toggle child links Activities & Organizations Athletics Health & Wellness Residence Life Leadership & Service Religious & Spiritual Life Campus Safety Dean of Students Belonging at LR Student Support & Outreach LR Experience Athletics About Click to toggle child links Fast Facts History & Traditions University Leadership Strategic Plan Accreditation Directory Offices & Services Community Partners Resources for Alumni Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Apply Visit Request Info Give Close Menu Home Page Admission and Aid Paying Your Bill Pay Your Deposit Pay Your Deposit Once you have been admitted to Lenoir-Rhyne, it’s time to reserve your place in the incoming class. To pay your deposit, you will need to log in with your application username and password. See the sections below for costs and how to pay your deposit. Questions regarding tuition payments can be directed to Student Accounts . Undergraduate Student Deposit The deposit to secure undergraduate enrollment is $300. If you have questions, please contact your admission counselor . The deposit to secure RIBN enrollment is $100. If you have questions, please contact our admission office at admission@lr.edu . Pay Your Undergraduate Programs Deposit Please note that the undergraduate enrollment deposit is non-refundable. Graduate Student Deposit The deposit to secure graduate enrollment is $200 for all programs, except: Doctor of Nursing Practice, DNP/FNP - $500 (non-refundable) Occupational Therapy, M.S. - $500 (non-refundable) Physician Assistant Studies, M.S. - $1,000 (non-refundable) Dietetic Internship Program - $200 (non-refundable) If you have questions, please contact your admission counselor . Please note that the graduate enrollment deposit is non-refundable. Pay Your Graduate Program's Deposit Seminarian Commitment Congratulations on your acceptance to Lutheran Theological Southern Seminary. Completing this form will indicate to us your decision to become the newest member of our community. Fill Out Your Seminary Commitment Office of Admission 510 7th Ave NE Hickory, NC 28601 admission@lr.edu 828.328.7382 Get Info Visit Apply Deposit Return to home Find us on Facebook Subscribe on YouTube Follow us on Instagram 625 7th Ave NE, Hickory, NC 28601 828.328.1741 Directory Virtual Tour, Maps & Directions Events Calendar University News Profile Magazine Work at LR Library Bookstore Copyright Privacy Policy Accessibility Title IX Safety & Emergency Preparedness Consumer Information Coronavirus © 2026 Lenoir-Rhyne University"
    }
